fact WorkItem(id: "WI-517", description: some(value: "Grammar: support type-annotated lambda binders (lambda (x: T) -> ..., lambda (acc: A, elem: B) -> ...). The parser currently REJECTS type annotations in lambda patterns: grammar.js _pattern = pattern_constructor/tuple/literal/wildcard/var has no 'name: Type' form, and pattern_tuple requires >=2 elements, so even a single typed binder '(u: Unit)' fails to parse ('syntax error near x: Int64'). kernel-language.md 4.7 DOCUMENTED these forms (lambda (u: Unit) -> body as the nullary-thunk recommendation; lambda (acc: A, elem: B) -> add(acc, elem) as typed tuple destructuring) but they were unparseable; the docs were corrected to match the grammar under WI-516 (nullary thunk = 'lambda () -> body'; lambda tuple binders untyped, types inferred from the expected arrow type). This WI restores the doc-intended FEATURE: allow optional ': Type' annotations on lambda binders. EMPIRICAL STATE (probed 2026-06-19): 'lambda x -> e' OK, 'lambda () -> e' OK (nullary thunk), 'lambda (a, b) -> e' OK (untyped tuple), 'lambda (x: T) -> e' PARSE ERROR, 'lambda (a: A, b: B) -> e' PARSE ERROR. SCOPE: tree-sitter-anthill/grammar.js (extend the lambda param pattern to accept typed binders -- a dedicated typed-binder pattern, or allow field_decl as a tuple element), regenerate parser (parser.c is gitignored, build regens), parse/convert.rs lowering to carry each annotation into the lambda param's type so it constrains inference, corpus tests (tree-sitter-anthill/test/corpus/expressions.txt) + a typer test that an annotated binder type-checks and conflicts LOUDLY on a body/annotation mismatch. Motivation: annotations let a lambda be written without an expected-type context (e.g. a bare 'let f = lambda (x: Int64) -> x') and document intent in foldLeft-style callbacks. Discovered while building the WI-516 graded Delay instance."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-19T16:11:09Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-517", name: "grammar")

